  "notes": {
    "c0001.md": "# Marguerite Okoye\n\nGood client, expensive habits. Decides fast in a meeting and reverses it by email\ntwo days later, which is how a 52 hour job turned into 75.\n\n- Rounds one and two were scope. Three, four and five were not.\n- The change order is written and unsent. It is worth about 4000.\n- She has already offered to introduce two other founders. Ask after launch, not\n  during the change order conversation.\n",
    "p0001.md": "# Okoye identity and store\n\nRed. Fixed at 12500. Ana took 4800, Theo took 1980, photography and type took\n1200. Studio time is 75 hours against 52 quoted.\n\nCosted at the studio rate this job loses money. It felt like the best work of the\nyear while it was happening, which is the point.\n\nWhat changes on the next one:\n\n- Two rounds in the quote, in writing, with a number attached to round three.\n- Subcontractor quotes locked before the client price, not after.\n- Product entry is the client's job or it is a line item.\n"
  }
